19	 To turn this off, call `native_tool_types(false)` on the builder. The adapter then sends the generic entry for every tool. A wrapper tool must forward `provider_types` from the tool it wraps, or the typed entry is lost.
20	 
21	 ## Extended thinking in a tool loop
22	 
23	 The stream keeps each `thinking` and `redacted_thinking` block as a `ContentPart::ProviderData` part with the key `PROVIDER_DATA_KEY`. The next request sends the blocks back unchanged for every assistant message in the history. The shape of the `data` is private to this crate.
24	 
25	 A thinking block is sent back only in the same assistant message as a text block or a `tool_use` block of its own response. If its response had `tool_use` blocks, one of them must be in that message. So after a hand-off that removed the tool calls of a response, or when the history lost those calls, the SDK sends no thinking block of that response. At the end of a history, the SDK sends no thinking block in a last assistant message. The cache never marks a thinking block as a breakpoint. A response with no kept thinking block writes no provider data.
26	 
27	 - For a 4.x model with `ExtendedThinking::Enabled`, add `.beta("interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14")` to the builder. Then the model can think again after a tool result.
28	 - `claude-sonnet-5-5` needs `ExtendedThinking::Adaptive`.
29	+- With `ExtendedThinking::Adaptive`, the provider sends `block_binding.prefix_mismatch_behavior = "drop_block"` and the beta header `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01`. If the history before a thinking block changed, the API drops that block and every later thinking block. The model loses that reasoning. The request does not fail. Examples are a hand-off with other `system` text or tools, and an edit of an earlier message.
30	+- With `ExtendedThinking::Enabled`, the provider sends no binding. Use `Enabled` only on models that do not run the prefix check, for example `claude-haiku-4-5`. Claude Opus 4.7 and later, Sonnet 5 and later, Haiku 5.5 and Fable reject `Enabled`.
31	 
32	 **Cost.** Each request sends the thinking blocks of the history again. We measured this on Claude Sonnet 4.5 and Opus 4.5 with `Enabled { budget_tokens: 2048 }`. It added about 100 input tokens to each round without the beta header. It added about 250 to 300 input tokens with the header.
33	 
34	 **Recovery.** Anthropic checks each signature. If it rejects one block, each later request of the session fails. To recover, remove every part with `provider == PROVIDER_DATA_KEY` from the stored history.
35	 
36	 **Privacy.** The thinking text is stored two times: as a `Reasoning` part and inside the provider data. A host that removes `Reasoning` must also remove the parts with this key. If a host removes these parts, the SDK cannot send the thinking blocks back.
37	 
