596	+## Prefix check (added after the local review)
597	+
598	+### Facts
599	+
600	+Two live probes on 2026-11-21 and the Claude API reference gave these facts.
601	+
602	+- Newer models run a history-editing check, also called the prefix check. These models are Sonnet 5.5, Opus 5.5, Haiku 5.5, and Fable 5.1 and 5.2.
603	+- A signature of a thinking block records the top-level `system` text, the `tools` set, and every message before the block. It also records a chain to the previous thinking block. A client can remove blocks from the front of the history. A client cannot remove blocks from the middle.
604	+- Accounts made on or after 2026-08-31 get an HTTP 400 when the prefix changed. The message is `messages.1.content.0: Invalid signature in thinking block. The block is bound to a different conversation.`
605	+- The request field `thinking.block_binding.prefix_mismatch_behavior: "drop_block"` needs the beta header `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01`. The API then drops the first mismatched block and every later thinking block. The request proceeds. The response has a top-level `input_transformations` array.
606	+- The API accepts `block_binding` only with `thinking.type: "adaptive"`. No model accepts it with `"enabled"`. Models that do not run the check also accept the object. A request with `block_binding` and no beta header gets a 400.
607	+- `claude-sonnet-4-5` is deprecated and retires on 2026-11-30. `Enabled { budget_tokens }` works on models before 4.6, for example `claude-haiku-4-5`. It works, deprecated, on Opus 4.6 and Sonnet 4.6. Opus 4.7, 4.8, 5 and 5.5, Sonnet 5 and 5.5, Haiku 5.5 and Fable reject it with a 400.
608	+
609	+### Probe result (claude-sonnet-5-5, drop_block)
610	+
611	+| Change before the second request | Result |
612	+| --- | --- |
613	+| Changed `system` | thinking block dropped |
614	+| Added a tool | thinking block dropped |
615	+| Changed a tool description | thinking block dropped |
616	+| Changed the text of the first user message | thinking block dropped |
617	+| Inserted a text block before the thinking block in the same message | thinking block dropped |
618	+| Edited or removed text after the thinking block in the same message | thinking block kept |
619	+| Unchanged tool loop | thinking block kept |
620	+
621	+### Decision
622	+
623	+Sven chose Option A. With `ExtendedThinking::Adaptive`, the provider sends `block_binding` with `prefix_mismatch_behavior: "drop_block"` and the beta header `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01`. The provider adds the header once, also when the user added it with `.beta(...)`. The provider sets extended thinking on the builder only, so the header follows the builder value. `Enabled` and `Disabled` send no binding.
624	+
625	+Sven rejected two other options. A prefix hash is complex and needs a byte-exact copy of the request prefix. Documentation only leaves the 400 error in place for hand-offs.
626	+
627	+With `Adaptive`, a changed prefix costs the model its earlier reasoning. The request does not fail.
